@startuml
title Game flow — engine and win condition

skinparam linetype ortho

/'
  No Phase enum. Nothing on a card reads the phase, and the engine's own
  method structure (setup, playTurn's steps) already is the phase. Add one,
  and a PhaseEntered event, when a card says "at the start of your Main phase".
'/
class TurnEngine {
    - battle: Battle
    + {static} MAX_TURNS: int = 30

    + playGame(): Optional<Side>
    + setup(): void
    + playTurn(): void
    /' Only ever for battle.attacker(): every ITarget is turn-relative, so
       there is deliberately no Side parameter. '/
    + legalActions(): List<IAction>
    + checkKnockouts(Optional<PokemonInPlay>): void
    + isOver(): boolean
    + winner(): Optional<Side>
}

note right of TurnEngine
  What legalActions offers, and the gate on each
  (every candidate is filtered by its own isLegal):

  **Action**             attacks of the active — cost satisfied,
                         not Asleep or Paralyzed
  **AttachEnergyAction** currentEnergy present and not yet
                         attached this turn
  **PlayCardAction**     hand cards playable now; at most one
                         Supporter per turn
  **EvolveAction**       evolution in hand, target played on an
                         earlier turn, and not turn 1 or 2 (no one
                         evolves on their first turn)
  **RetreatAction**      retreat cost payable, bench not empty,
                         not Asleep or Paralyzed
  **UseAbilityAction**   activated abilities not yet used
  **EndTurnAction**      always
end note

note bottom of TurnEngine
  **Win conditions** — each counts once per side:
   * **points**: at least 3 points
   * **bench**: you have Pokemon in play and your opponent has none

  The game ends as soon as either side holds one. The side holding
  MORE conditions wins; equal counts are a tie. So a double KO that
  takes you to 3 points but leaves you nothing to promote, while
  your opponent still has a bench, is a tie (points vs bench).

  After turn MAX_TURNS (30) the game is a tie.
end note

TurnEngine *-- Battle
TurnEngine ..> IPlayer
TurnEngine ..> TriggerDispatcher

@enduml

@startuml
title Game flow — setup

start
note right
  The caller builds each Side (deck, registered energy
  types) and passes them to Battle(first, second) in
  turn order: the first-player coin flip is the caller's.
end note
repeat :for each side;
  if (deck holds no Basic?) then (yes)
    :throw IllegalStateException;
    stop
  endif
  :shuffle until the top 5 hold a Basic;
  :draw 5;
  :owner CHOOSES the Active from Basics in hand;
  :owner CHOOSES Bench Pokemon one at a time
   (empty = done), up to BENCH_LIMIT;
repeat while (more sides?)
stop

@enduml

@startuml
title Game flow — one turn

start
:dispatch TurnStart;
:draw 1 card;
note right: deck-out is not a loss in Pocket

if (turn 1?) then (yes)
  :no energy for the first player;
else (no)
  :generateEnergy;
endif

repeat
  :options = legalActions();
  :chosen = player.choose(Decision<IAction>(options));
  :chosen.execute(ctx);
  note right
    An attack announces itself: Action.execute dispatches
    AttackDeclared, which is where Confusion vetoes it.
  end note
  :checkKnockouts(attacker's active if chosen was an attack);
  if (game over?) then (yes)
    stop
  endif
repeat while (chosen was an attack or EndTurnAction?) is (no) not (yes)

:dispatch TurnEnd;
note right
  Poison, Burn, Sleep and Paralysis are TurnEnd
  triggers on the statuses — no engine step for them.
end note
:checkKnockouts(empty);
if (game over?) then (yes)
  stop
endif

:expire ActiveModifiers not live next turn;
:reset per-turn flags on both Sides;
:battle.switchSides() (turn++);
stop

@enduml

@startuml
title Game flow — checkKnockouts

start
repeat :for each knocked-out Pokemon, both sides;
  :opponent scores 3 for MEGA_EX, 2 for EX, else 1;
  :dispatch Knockout;
  note right
    While still in play, so the Pokemon's own
    Tool and ability can react to it.
  end note
  :remove from play; discard every card in its
   evolution stack and its tool (attached energy
   simply goes);
repeat while (anything still knocked out? a Knockout trigger may deal damage)

if (either side holds a win condition?) then (yes)
  :game over — most conditions wins, equal is a tie;
  stop
endif

:each side with no Active CHOOSES a replacement
 from its bench (defender first);
stop

@enduml
